  "strategy": "1 Approach and Rationale\nStart by optimizing the core convolution kernel via iterative refinement. The key innovation involves introducing variable-height spikes guided by autocorrelation feedback. We'll use difference-of-constraints optimization (a mixed-integer approach) to enforce non-negativity while seeking minimal peak autocorrelation through Lagrangian duality. This differs from the previous Gaussian initialization by incorporating active constraint set analysis from weighted-L1 regularizations.\n\n2 Mathematical Specification\nConsider a sequence a of length n. The optimization is over two dimensions:\n- Integer-variable 'k' spike counts via combinatorics\n- Continuous-variable smoothing parameters 't' and 'w'\nDefine auxiliary variables:\n- b_j = a_j for all j\n- c_ij = the autocorrelation contribution\nThe objective function is J(a) = (2*n)/(sum(a)^2)*max(convolve(a,a))\nConstraints: a_j \u2265 0 for all j, sum(a) > 0.01\n\n3 Implementation Procedure\nInitialize using local minima achieved through:\n  1. Soft penalty scaling to any starting point\n  2. Simplex reflection for high-dimensionality\nThen, schedule:\n  for l in 1 to 5 (search magnitude):\n      for s in range(steps):\n          Space allocate 3ms per element evaluation\n          Gradually introduce combinatorial integer constraints\n          Apply gradient descent with dimension-dependent learning rates\n\n4 Search Choices\nWe'll employ:\n  lag_ratio = 0.8 (default)\n  w=0.4, t=0.5 as base parameters\nFive phases: 1) Basic optimization, 2) Persistent tuning, 3) Coarser sampling, 4) Focused refinement, 5) Dimension expansion\n\n5 Compute Budget\nEstimate dominance with n=4096 around 40ms, requiring up to 2048 iterations\nZero out gradient components outside validate zones\n\n6 Validation and Return Contract\nMust check gradient descent termination conditions and enforce soft constraints\nThe training phase includes ensuring sequence expansion always maintains positivity (using exponential weighting)",
